# For deploying the adguard stack BY HAND. From Komodo, put the same lines in
# the Stack's Environment instead (see "AdGuard Home" in the README).
#
# Copy to stack.env (gitignored), fill in, and load into the shell before
# deploying -- stack deploy reads the environment, not this file:
#
#   set -a; . apps/adguard/stack.env; set +a
#   docker stack deploy -c apps/adguard/compose.yml adguard
#
# Sourced by the shell, so anything with a $ in it goes in single quotes.

# Web UI login, as a bcrypt htpasswd line. Applied on every start, so this is
# also how you change the password later:
#   docker run --rm httpd:alpine htpasswd -nbB admin 'your-password'
ADGUARD_AUTH=''

# First start only -- after that, change these in the web UI.
# ADGUARD_UPSTREAMS='https://dns.cloudflare.com/dns-query https://dns.google/dns-query'
# ADGUARD_ALLOWED_CLIENTS='100.64.0.0/10 fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 127.0.0.0/8 ::1'

# DOMAIN=liaxum.fr
# ADGUARD_SUBDOMAIN=adguard
# MANAGER_HOSTNAME=liaxum-vps
# TZ=Europe/Paris
